    "claims: each names a pattern (assets/Name-*.js) rather than the hash of the day, because these are the durable half of the spec — a panel's literals survive a rebuild. A present claim holds only if every string is in one of the named files; an absent claim holds only if none of them is.",
    "Anything with an '*' in files is resolved against what the entry page and its bundles currently name, so a renamed chunk is found instead of silently skipped."
